ick is worth to you  and then google looks at your bid in the  relevancy of your ads  and they do this for all the other  advertisers as well then they  order the ads and the search results  were across display properties  based upon both the bid and the  relevancy  now this is an important consideration  as useful ads  are as important as your bids in  determining position  so we'll get into this later when we  look at organization  now it's not just who bids the most that  will get you into position one  is your ad relevant to the user  there's a lot of ways to make things  relevant and we'll walk through this  later  if a user sees your ad you don't pay  anything  only if a user clicks on your ad  do you pay the search engine that's why  it's called pay  per click advertising because you only  pay when someone clicks on the ad  now you can then measure results such as  acquired customers return on ad spend  revenue and so forth  now based upon the results you're  receiving from google ads  you can then refine your ads or change  your bids  based upon what those clicks are worth  to you  when we think about the google ads  benefits we often call them  the three r's reach relevance  roi now from a reach standpoint google  search  and the display networks have tremendous  reach they can help you reach your  target  audience because your target audience is  probably using google whether it's on  search or display or both  so the advertising system has the reach  that  encompasses your potential customers the  next  think about relevance this is a big  thing in advertising  are you relevant to the users  searches are often resistant to ads  that's why if you're watching tv and a  commercial appears  you might hit the fast forward button or  switch the channel when the ad  is relevant users like ads  they'll interact with them if they're  useful and  they're relevant so you can target users  based upon  many criteria which means your ad should  be relevant to users especially on  search when you pick keywords that  represent  your business as someone is actively  searching for that word  that means they're looking for a  solution so when users see relevant ads  they're more likely to click and do  business with your company  now finally we have roi known as return  on investment  as our third benefit return ad spend row  os or roi  let us know how profitable a channel  is now as you can measure results from  your ad spend  you can make data driven decisions based  upon how users  interact with your ads and how they're  becoming customers  so google ads has the reach that  encompasses your users  when you make good accounts and you have  good account structure  which we'll get into later videos you  can ensure your ad is  relevant to users so they'll click on  the ads  and come to your website so you can turn  them into customers  now with analytics and conversion  tracking you can see  exactly how much that person's worth to  you  so then you can adjust your reach and  your relevance data  to ensure that your return on investment  is fantastic from using  google ads as a marketing channel so  google ads accounts have multiple  levels of structure in order for you to  be able to control how users can  view interact with your ads along with  your budget and bid controls  now in this lesson we'll examine each  level of hierarchy  so you can understand how average  accounts fit together  and how data flows throughout your  accounts so by the end of this lesson  you're able to understand account level  settings  understand campaign targeting options  and discuss the purpose of an ad group  so when we look at the overall account  hierarchy it starts  where we have an account then an account  can be made  of one or more campaigns then each  campaign  can have one or more ad groups and then  finally  ad groups are a collection of ads and  keywords so as we look at accounts  campaigns and ad groups  each level has different items you set  with it  so we're going to look individually at  each of these items  to see how you can use various settings  at each level  now at the account level we have several  options that we can set  the first is account access this is who  can log in and access your data  so when you open an account you'll use a  google account  the list doesn't have to be a gmail  address you can make your own email  address for your company  a google account and then use that for  login purposes  but then you can give others access to  your account as well  from a security standpoint it's useful  just to have one  administrator who gives access levels to  other individuals  that way if someone leaves your company  or no longer needs access to your data  you can disable just that access point  instead of using  shared account logins now you'll also  choose your time zone  now some items such as time zone and  currency cannot be  changed once you open the account so you  pick your time zone  and when you think about it you it's  useful to have your analytics  your server and your marketing such as  your google ads account  on the same time zone now because if  you've got an  ads account in pacific time and your  servers on  eastern time there's a three hour period  of time a day when your data doesn't  agree with each other  so it's useful to sync servers google  ads account  analytics so forth into a single time  zone now you'll also choose your  currency  do you want to be billed in euros or  dollars or pounds or canadian dollars  and so forth  again currency can't be changed once  you've set up your account as well  and then you have billing how are you  going to pay for the clicks that you  accrue  and then you can connect other accounts  to your google ads account  such as google analytics google merchant  center firebase etc  so if you're using multiple systems you  can connect them  all together at the account level so  they can all use the same data  and then you have notification settings  how do you want to be notified of  suggestions or disapproved ads and so  forth  in some preferences like display  language  number formats etc so that when you open  an account  the two most important options really to  think about though are time zone and  currency  they can't be changed you can change  your billing later on or you can change  his account access and preferences but  time zone and currency  are set once your account is open let's  look at the campaign settings  you have an account an account can be  made up of one  or more campaigns so a campaign setting  is where you're going to tell google ads  how to  show the ads and keywords within that  campaign  so first we have the network do you want  to be on search network display network  or potentially both  and when you're first starting search is  the best place to start because users  are  actively looking for solutions  so you could have one campaign that  searched and another campaign that is  displayed  now we choose our devices at the  campaign level as well so it might be on  all devices we could be on just mobile  devices or just computers or just  tablets  if we want to run our ads at certain  times of day  or day of the week we also set those and  the campaign  settings so if you only want your ads to  run monday to friday  you can choose those options at the  campaign level  now is say you want your brand terms to  run all of the time  and then you have other keywords you  only want to run monday to friday  then you can use two campaigns campaigns  can have different settings from each  other  so you could have one campaign for your  legion keywords that runs monday to  friday  clicks go to a call center you can maybe  have  another campaign that's brand terms that  runs  all seven days of the week and they're  in another campaign  so that way you can segment out which  items run when  now locations are also set up at the  campaign setting  so if you're a multi-location business