n you  want these campaign  level settings to be different that's  one of the main reasons to create  a new campaign for the ads and keywords  that are inside of that campaign now ad  groups are a collection  of keywords and ads and only an ad from  that  ad group that contains the same keyword  that matched to a search query  right can be displayed so ad groups  should be  closely related collections of keywords  and ads  so we think about the work involved and  setting up a google ads account  it's really quick just to make an  account it can be very quick to make a  campaign  but where you're going to slow down and  spend your time  is thinking about your ad groups someone  did a search they are looking for  something  they're going to then see an ad so that  ad is going to take them to a page of  your website  so you want that user experience be very  cohesive  so you may have one campaign the  campaign could have  20 or 50 or a thousand aggregates in it  right for each type of idea that you're  advertising  so if you want to show a user a  different  ad based upon their search term changing  you want a different ad group let's say  we sell shoes  now we sell hiking boots we sell running  shoes we sell dress shoes  now we don't want to do is put all of  those in one  ad group because if someone searches for  hiking boots versus  a running shoe versus a dress shoe  you want a different ad there's not a  good ad that explains  all those concepts so we could write an  ad  shoes for sale right but choose for sale  doesn't really speak to the user  if someone's doing a search for hiking  boots  right and they see an end that says  shoes for sale and another ad that says  hiking boots for sale right walk on the  trails  comfortably right they're gonna look at  the one  that says shoes for sale and say it's  not relevant to what i'm looking for  and the ad that mentioned the product  they search for hiking boots  would be relevant we get a lot more of  those clicks and conversions  so why we may take some keywords like  hiking boots  trail hiking boot hiking boots for sale  best hiking boots  and put them in an ad group together  right we make an  ad only for those keywords so we create  and add hiking boots for sale  walk the trails in comfort but then  someone searches for  running shoes that ad would not be a  good result for them  right hiking boots an ad that they're  looking for running shoes  so you'd want a different ad group for  running shoes  so you might have keywords running shoes  best running shoes shoes for running  marathon long distance running shoes  right and then we can make an ad that  says running shoes for sale  maximize your performance now if we were  really focused on running shoes and that  was our core  business then we wouldn't want to run  just a running shoe ad because that's  very general we want to get  more specific if someone's running a  marathon  they want long distance running shoes  others want  minimalistic running shoes you'll see  see people search for running shoes with  high arches  or better art support wide box shoes  so you can even get into those very  specific terms to create ads for them  in the ad groups when you think about ad  group structure  only the keywords and that ad group can  show for that  ad right if we have two ad groups  and someone searches for running shoes  right they can't see our  hiking boots ad because it's in a  different ad group they only see the  running shoes at so you can make  multiple ads in an ad group and do some  ad testing  to see which is best so if we look at an  ad group and we see here's another  keyword  that we really want to look at and the  ads we have  aren't great for that keyword we can  move it to a new  ad group so we may have one ad group set  stress shoes another for high heels  and we can make new adders for all of  these items  so that the ad and then where the user  goes on your website or  is specific to each of those types that  idea of keywords  so you might have many aggregates but  the trick about ad groups  is you have a core set of keywords in  each ad group  and then you have multiple ads in an ad  group and so as long as  all the ads and the keywords are  reflective of each other  then you've got a good ad group now if  an ad does not represent a  keyword that keyword should be in a  different ad aggregate  settings are inherited downwards across  the account  so for instance the account level you  set billing the billing methods used by  all the campaigns in the account  and all the ad groups so you set access  level by account so anyone with account  access level can see are your campaigns  in ad groups  so then at the campaign level we enter  settings like budgets location  so that goes from the campaign level is  inherited down to the ad groups  so any ad group in the campaign that can  show  to all the users in a location that's  set at the campaign level or budgets and  so forth  so then that goes from campaign is  inherited to the ad groups  so any aggro in the campaign can show  where it may  reach the campaign setting such as  location or it uses that same budget  where all the aggregate campaign use a  budget so if we have  different campaigns then only the ad  groups in that campaign  would use that campaign's budget and  that campaign's targeting  method so when you create a setting at  the account level  it's used at the campaign level and then  anything at the campaign level  is used at the ad group level so if you  create ad group level  settings for something you can set up  the ad group they're only used by the  ads and keywords  in that specific ad group ad group data  is  never inherited to another ad group  so setting hierarchy flows downwards  across the account from account to  campaign to ad group  and then the ads and keywords so the  first step to getting started with  google ads  is opening an account now once you open  an account  then you can fill in your billing  information add additional users  and connect your analytics account to  your google ads account  so in this lesson we will look at how to  create the initial account  now by the end of this lesson you'll be  able to open  a google ads account set permission  levels  and user access data and then connect  additional accounts  now before you begin creating a google  ads account  you'll need a google account to access  it  if you use gmail then you can use your  gmail  account if you want to use your business  email  then you can create an account and use  your business email address  you'll need to verify your account  through a text message code or through  an email to the email address  you're using to access your google ads  account now once you've established  how to access your google ads account  proceed to setting up your first  campaign  each person who can access your data  should have their own  login this lets you choose their  permission level  remove someone when they should no  longer have access  and see what changes were made in the  change history tool  which logs changes by user access  before adding a user you should consider  the permission  level that the user needs so for  instance  if you want someone to see information  but not change anything  you can give them read only access  if you want a user to be able to make  any changes  but not add or move other users they can  have standard access  by giving each user access you can  maintain control over your data  and also add and remove other users  as your need for accessing your data  changes  there are times when you will want your  google ads account  to connect with other applications so  they can share  data back and forth this is really  common with google analytics  by connecting google analytics and  google ads  you can see a lot of data in both places  in addition you can create conversions  or  audience lists in google analytics and  have them  imported into google ads if 